 "structural_change": "QE3-HROOT-PROMPT 10-21 successor of n34a/n34b: SOURCE ps4 native32 (qkd_hr_core_prompt_mu4p4_n32, sha 09028f6e, census max32) = ps3 + capture flops DIRECTLY on every used SRAM rd_out (RX + completion-event queues via ot_hkv_prompt_mem_r with the read address from the registered head pointer: no macro->macro path; 4 program macros p_qr) -> macro->flop = clk->q + wire; +2 edges queue visibility, +1 program edge (static). io_flop_at_pins macro_out_pins rd_out anchors the capture flops at the macro pins. CLOCK: n34a measured recipe (pin flops anchored at their faces, boundary on its own balanced+equalised branch bnd_branch.tcl, stem at ck_core beside the central register band; n34a 58.1/55.3 ps). FALLBACK: ENLARGED outline 518.4x475.2 (fill ~35%), macro channels >=20 um everywhere (the abutted 4x 256x64 stack becomes a 2x2 with 41.7/25.4 um channels), 81 um central column between the 32x546 pair.",
 "reroute_reason": {
  "kind": "rtl_change",
  "reason": "n34b FAIL (spread 102/100, macro->reg -399, macro->macro -301); n34a placed macro->reg -397: ps4 registered SRAM read outputs."
 },
 "slot_change_request": "UNGRANTED: outline [518.4, 475.2]; parent repack needed.",
 "safe_design_checklist": {
  "1_pins": "SOURCE: every non-reset pin registered (flow pin regs in the ps4 synth), por_n 2-stage landing; ports/order unchanged; faces <=75%.",
  "2_reach": "pin flops anchored at faces, pin->logic <= ~240 um; rd_out capture flops anchored at the macro pins.",
  "3_fanout": "native32 census max32 (regenerated; gate re-checks).",
  "4_depth": "macro->flop = clk->q + wire (no logic); header compare/consume reg->reg; read address from a register (no macro->macro).",
  "5_storage": "7 real SRAM macros; std bands between macro rows.",
  "6_floorplan": "fill ~41% (n35a) / ~35% (n35b enlarged); enlarge-not-squeeze.",
  "7_clock": "boundary own balanced+equalised branch, pin flops grouped by face (n34a measured 58.1/55.3 <=80).",
  "8_reset": "control/valid-only reset; queue tag/valid regs reset, capture data flops reset-free."
 },
